1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,210
23点59分60秒，
23:59:60.

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:04,050
以后再也看不到了。
You'll never see it again.

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:05,150
不是钟坏了，
The clock isn't broken.

4
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:07,670
是全世界刚投票取消了闰秒。
The world just voted to scrap the leap second.

5
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:09,220
国际计量大会决定：
The General Conference on Weights and Measures decided:

6
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:12,460
2027年5月20日起，不再插闰秒。
from May 20, 2027, no more leap seconds.

7
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:15,000
今天的问题：钟和地球对不上，
Today's question: clocks and Earth disagree.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,750
为什么不等地球了？
Why stop waiting for Earth?

9
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:17,990
先认识小地，
Meet Little Earth.

10
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:20,370
它每转一圈，就是一天。
One spin is one day.

11
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:23,060
再认识小铯，原子钟里的铯原子，
And Little Cesium, the atom inside an atomic clock:

12
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,160
一秒振动九十一亿多次。
over 9.1 billion wiggles a second.

13
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,320
最好的铯钟，
The best cesium clocks

14
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,370
三亿年都差不到一秒。
wouldn't lose a second in 300 million years.

15
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:30,860
1967年起，一秒有多长，
Since 1967, the length of a second

16
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:32,510
就由小铯说了算。
has been set by cesium.

17
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:34,780
问题来了：小铯从来不偷懒，
Here's the problem: cesium never slacks,

18
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:36,290
小地却时快时慢。
but Earth speeds up and slows down.

19
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:38,100
月亮的潮汐像刹车片，
The Moon's tides act like brake pads,

20
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,670
一点点拖慢地球。
slowly dragging Earth down.

21
00:00:39,670 --> 00:00:41,650
冰川融化，水流向赤道，
Melting ice flows toward the equator,

22
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:44,650
就像滑冰的人张开胳膊，转得更慢。
like a skater opening her arms and slowing down.

23
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:46,920
地核晃一晃、刮几场大风，
A wobble in the core, a few big winds,

24
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,320
一天的长短也会差几毫秒。
and a day changes by milliseconds.

25
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:50,550
所以“一天”，
So a day

26
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,130
其实并不正好是86400秒。
isn't exactly 86,400 seconds.

27
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:54,330
差多了怎么办？
So what do you do when they drift apart?

28
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:57,010
1972年起，人们发明了闰秒。
In 1972, people invented the leap second.

29
00:00:57,010 --> 00:00:58,730
钟跑到地球前面了，
When the clock gets ahead of Earth,

30
00:00:58,730 --> 00:01:01,530
就在午夜多插一秒，等等地球。
add one second at midnight and let Earth catch up.

31
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:03,430
到现在一共插了27次，
It's been done 27 times,

32
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:06,150
最近一次是2016年最后一天。
most recently on the last day of 2016.

33
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:08,320
每次都是全世界同一时刻，
Each time, the whole world

34
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,880
一起多等这一秒。
waits that extra second at the same moment.

35
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:10,580
反转一：
Twist one:

36
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:12,620
这一秒，把电脑坑惨了。
that one second wrecked computers.

37
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:14,330
电脑只认到59秒，
Computers count to 59.

38
00:01:14,330 --> 00:01:17,110
突然冒出个60秒，直接懵了。
Suddenly there's a 60, and they freeze.

39
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:18,800
2012年那次闰秒，
In the 2012 leap second,

40
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:22,480
好几家大网站和航空公司订票系统都出了故障。
big websites and an airline booking system broke.

41
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,820
2017年元旦，
On New Year's Day 2017,

42
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:26,960
一家大型网络公司也因为闰秒短暂出错。
a major internet company glitched because of one.

43
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:29,120
有的公司干脆发明了“抹秒”，
Some companies invented the leap smear,

44
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:30,940
把这一秒摊进一整天里。
spreading that second across a whole day.

45
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:33,050
5G基站、电网、金融交易，
5G towers, power grids, stock trades:

46
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:34,620
时间一秒都不能乱。
they can't afford a messy second.

47
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:35,270
反转二：
Twist two:

48
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:37,160
地球这几年反而转快了！
lately, Earth has been spinning faster!

49
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:38,630
人们甚至开始讨论，
People even started talking about

50
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:40,700
要不要第一次“减”一秒。
taking a second away for the first time.

51
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,900
负闰秒就是直接跳过一秒，
A negative leap second skips a second entirely.

52
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,400
从来没人试过，谁也不敢试。
Nobody has ever tried it, and nobody wants to.

53
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,320
原本估算2026年前后就得减一秒，
One estimate said we'd need it around 2026.

54
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:51,520
冰川融化把它推迟到了2029年前后。
Melting ice pushed that back to around 2029.

55
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,080
所以干脆：不插了，
So the decision: stop adding them,

56
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,590
让钟只管自己走。
and let the clocks just tick.

57
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:56,160
钟和地球的误差，
The allowed gap between clock and Earth

58
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:59,210
放宽到3600秒，整整一小时。
grows to 3600 seconds. A full hour.

59
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:01,830
反转三：那太阳会不会越来越不准？
Twist three: will the Sun drift off schedule?

60
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,750
会，但慢得你察觉不到。
Yes, too slowly to notice.

61
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:05,860
按近几十年的速度估算，
At the pace of recent decades,

62
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:08,080
攒满一小时，要上千年。
filling that hour would take over a thousand years.

63
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,580
说白了，这一小时，
In other words, that hour

64
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,020
留给几百上千年后的人去操心。
is a problem for people centuries from now.

65
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,880
一辈子下来，太阳也就晚个把分钟，
In a lifetime, the Sun might run a minute or so late.

66
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,430
你根本感觉不到。
You'd never feel it.

67
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:18,440
北斗导航也松了口气：
Navigation satellites relax too:

68
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:21,360
不用再处理闰秒，换算少出错。
no leap seconds means fewer conversion errors.

69
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,550
说到底，是两种时间在打架：
In the end, it's two kinds of time fighting:

70
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:25,350
天文时间和原子时间。
Earth time and atom time.

71
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:26,850
以前是钟等地球，
Before, the clock waited for Earth.

72
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:29,420
以后是钟先走，地球慢慢跟。
Now the clock walks on, and Earth follows slowly.

73
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:32,240
友情提示：天文学家用的世界时还在，
Friendly fine print: astronomers' Earth time still exists,

74
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,850
太阳照样东升西落。
and the Sun still rises in the east.

75
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:35,810
这事也不影响你的闹钟，
Your alarm clock won't notice either.

76
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:37,530
手机照样自动对时。
Your phone still syncs itself.

77
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:40,240
所以最后一个23点59分60秒，
So the last 23:59:60

78
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,220
已经留在了2016年。
stays forever in 2016.

79
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:44,760
小地慢慢转，小铯一秒不差，
Earth spins at its own pace, cesium never misses,

80
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,450
从此各走各的，相安无事。
and from now on, they each go their own way.

